# vscode-delete-dialog-enter-cancels-silently — the half that is still open.
#
# The finding has two halves. Enter NOT deleting is now deliberate: the fix
# (387d7a9c) was reverted by fcb8b5e6, and src/app/trash.zig:234 says why —
# "Cancel is the focus, as in Rust: a destructive box's Enter must not be
# the destructive act". That half is by-design and this script does not
# contest it.
#
# The SILENT half has no stated rationale anywhere. A user who presses Enter
# on "Delete a.txt?" gets the dialog torn down with no toast and no
# statusline line — indistinguishable on screen from a delete that worked.
# This asserts only that the cancel announces itself. It fails on main.
write a.txt "aa"
command view.focus_tree
key r
key end
command file.delete
expect screen contains "Delete a.txt?"
key enter
wait 400
# the by-design half — the file survives. This passes today.
expect file a.txt contains "aa"
# the open half — the app must say the delete did not happen.
expect screen contains "cancel"
